description:
**The Job**

We are looking for a Creative Director Product to lead and shape the future of our product categories across some of the most relevant global A-brands in sport and fashion.

As a trusted long-term licensing partner, we have built global brand collaborations over decades — translating brand DNA into commercially successful, consumer-relevant products at scale. This role sits at the heart of that model: connecting brand vision, creative direction, and exceptional product execution.

You will define a clear product vision, inspire your team, and translate global brand strategies into standout category concepts — from technically advanced first-layer products (socks, bodywear & underwear) to high-impact fanwear collections linked to the world’s leading teams and assets.

**Your Mission**

* Define and drive a creative product strategy and long-term vision across all categories;
* Translate brand and company strategy into compelling product concepts and seasonal roadmaps;
* Bring brand DNA and storytelling to life through commercially relevant product design;
* Lead the development of technically strong, best-in-class first-layer products;
* Drive product execution at scale, delivering high-volume, commercially successful assortments;
* Ensure products deliver on best price–value ratio, balancing design, quality and cost;
* Anticipate and translate consumer needs and trends into relevant assortments;
* Ensure we are present where the consumer shops, delivering the right product for the right channel;

Fanwear (integrated scope):


* Lead the creation of fanwear collections for top-tier teams, translating partnerships into commercially successful products;
* Operate within a triangle partnership model (brand – team – stichd) to ensure strong alignment and execution;
* Drive fast, responsive product execution around key moments, turning speed into a differentiator ;
* Translate real-time consumer insights (e.g. trackside, DTC) into scalable products that meet fan expectations;
* Build focused assortments and capsule drops that drive engagement, conversion and sell-through.

**Your Talent**

You bring the creative vision, product instinct and commercial sharpness to shape collections that move at the speed of culture — and perform in the real world.




**You have:**  

* 10+ years of experience in a senior creative or product leadership role within sport, fashion, lifestyle or a connected consumer goods environment;
* A proven track record of working with global brands, preferably within a licensing, partnership or brand-led product environment;
* Strong experience in building multi-year product visions and translating them into clear seasonal strategies, concepts and roadmaps;
* A deep understanding of technical product development, ideally within first-layer categories such as socks, bodywear and underwear;
* Experience creating high-volume, commercially successful product ranges that balance brand heat, consumer relevance, qual

**The Job**

The Product Management department oversees the end-to-end product process, ensuring the full collection is delivered on time. As Product Manager, you align the collection with market needs and the stichd strategy by connecting internal processes and creative teams. You act as the central coordinator across Product Development, Product Design, Operations, Marketing, and Sales.


Working with a brand focus across several product groups, you translate product needs for different distribution channels and manage key account requests.

**Your Mission**

* Execute and manage the product process from clear briefs to range launch;

* Create a lineplan and planning and translate this effectively into a clear product briefing for the creative team and coordinate the tasks and responsibilities of the teams;

* Develop short- and long-term collection strategies, tactical product executions and innovations that position our brands as the leaders in the assigned categories;

* Prepare market- and competitor studies on an international level as well as analyzing forecasts and sales data;

* Cooperate with design, development, and sales to ensure final collections reflect market needs;

* Collaborate with stakeholders and drive the product creation process based on the Go-to-Market calendar milestones;

* Understand sales, margin, and merchandising requirements to deliver market / account fitting product concepts;

* Meet category financial targets as set by the organization;

* Manage, maintain, and distribute all information of assigned product lines. Ensuring correct and on time input in PLM (Product Lifecycle Management) and ERP system;

* Present product lines to internal and external teams in a comprehensive, clear, tactical manner.

**Your Talent**

* Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, Fashion Management, or a related field;

* At least four years of product management experience, preferably in sports lifestyle, sporting goods, or an international organization working with global brands;

* Strong knowledge of the lifestyle, fashion, and/or sporting goods markets, with a sharp commercial mindset and a solid understanding of sales drivers, retail dynamics, and competitor activity;

* Experience in close-to-body product categories is preferred;

* Flexible and open-minded team player with strong organizational, analytical, and prioritization skills;

* Clear and confident communicator with excellent written and spoken English;

* Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, Word, and PowerPoint.




This role is based in Den Bosch, the Netherlands. Working remotely from other countries is not possible.

To apply for this role, you must already have the legal right to work in the Netherlands. We will not apply for work or residence permits.





